Because the true values of conditional marker outcome probabilities are often not exactly known in advance, applying fixed parameters might be invalid. In this case, the Bayesian approach provides a way to contain expert prior knowledge concerning parameters. On the other hand, Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) applied to sample from the distribution of the model parameters. In this work, the autocorrelation plots and Geweke's statistic were utilized to check the convergence of Markov chains. Also, since no prior information on the parameters is available, non-informative prior distributions were used for all the parameters (i.e., a beta prior for
